llowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2020-04-19T01:45:53Z","label":{"name":"untriaged","color":"c34ddd"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/694241827","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11151#issuecomment-694241827","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/11151","id":694241827,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY5NDI0MTgyNw==","user":{"login":"janakdr","id":10134896,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM0ODk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10134896?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr","html_url":"https://github.com/janakdr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-09-17T13:39:32Z","updated_at":"2020-09-17T13:39:32Z","body":"Unfortunately this would be a bit tricky to fix in general. At the time an action fails, we may not know which outputs are needed (we know at least one is needed). In the case that A produces two outputs, A_important and A_unimportant, if B and C both depend on A, B runs first, and requests A_unimportant, while C would request A_important but hasn't yet executed in the build (because of scheduling) we'd still probably want to show the failure message with A_important.\r\n\r\nBesides that issue, technically this would be somewhat tricky to implement. The message comes from [SkfyrameActionExecutor](https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/blob/cfe91cef9f2473836d2f8a64cdbeda84ec9ed442/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/skyframe/SkyframeActionExecutor.java#L1598), I think. The knowledge of what other actions depend on this action, and in particular which artifact is needed, is not available there. We could potentially do some kind of retrieval of the other actions, check their inputs, and use the first output that was in those inputs, but it would be pretty complex.\r\n\r\nThe overall idea here is to tell the user what action failed to execute. I think we could add the action description (like, \"Compiling foo.cc\") to the error message. Would that be helpful?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/694241827/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"janakdr","id":10134896,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM0ODk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10134896?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr","html_url":"https://github.com/janakdr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/janakdr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/